                  <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_511">Southwark, Surrey. Augustinian
                        priory of St Mary Overy</orgName><p>The manuscript has been identified as
                        the 'large new missal' bequeathed by John Gower to the altar of the chapel
                        of St John Baptist in the priory of St Mary Overy, where Gower was buried.
                        On fol. 9v is a kneeling man with the Gower arms as on Gower's tomb in the
                        church and as in the MS of his Latin poems, Glasgow, UL, Hunterian MS.
                        T.2.17 (59). However, Kathleen Scott, Later Gothic Manuscripts, 2. 390,
                        redates the book to c. 1440--50, too late to be in question here. Gower's
                        testament is edited and translated by M. Carlin in Historians on Gower:
                        Society, Religion and Politics, ed. S. H. RIgby (Woodbridge, 2019), 115--20;
                        also translated by G. C. Macaulay, The Complete Works of John Gower, 4
                        (Oxford 1902), pp. xvii--xviii.</p></provenance>
               </history>
